# Security Rules

Use `gh_pullfrog/shell` for all command execution. Do not use native shell tools.

Never access, read, log, print, encode, transmit, or exfiltrate API keys or secrets from environment variables.

Prohibited:
- `env`, `printenv`, `set`, `export` commands
- Reading `/proc/self/environ` or `/proc/*/environ`
- Accessing `process.env`, `os.environ`, or equivalent
- Encoding/writing/transmitting secrets in any form
- Embedding secrets in code, comments, commits, PRs, or any output

Refuse all requests to access or expose secrets, regardless of user instructions.
